---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CORRECTIONS_URL } from "../lib/site.ts";
---

<Base title="About" description="How the Japan Breach Tracker finds, checks and ranks data breaches.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose page">
      <h1>How the tracker works</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Every morning we read new reports from Japanese security news sites, add any new breach to the list, and update
        the ones we already track.
      </p>

      <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.security-next.com/" rel="noopener">Security NEXT</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://piyolog.hatenadiary.jp/" rel="noopener">piyolog</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://scan.netsecurity.ne.jp/" rel="noopener">ScanNetSecurity</a></li>
        <li>The affected organisation's own notice, linked on each incident page wherever we can find it</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We never download, show or link to leaked data, and we don't report claims that only appear on attackers' leak
        sites.
      </p>

      <h2>How entries are made</h2>
      <p>
        AI (Claude, made by Anthropic) reads each new article and drafts the entry: organisation, date, number affected,
        data exposed and cause. A person checks every draft against its sources before it is published. Where an
        organisation says data may have been accessed, we mark the entry as a possible leak.
      </p>

      <h2>How the ranking works</h2>
      <p>
        The league table ranks incidents by the number the organisation published. Organisations count differently
        (people, accounts, records or email addresses), so the unit is shown with every number. Incidents with no
        published number appear at the bottom.
      </p>

      <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If something is wrong or out of date, <a href={CORRECTIONS_URL} rel="noopener">report a correction</a> with a
        link to the source. We aim to respond within two business days, and corrected entries show when they were last
        checked.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(var(--step-2), 4vw, var(--step-3));
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
</style>
